WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
Heating systems keep people alive in winter. You need to know them cold.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Electric heat uses resistance elements called heat strips. Nichrome wire
generates heat when current flows through it. Strips are staged through a
sequencer relay to prevent inrush current. A 15kW system might have three 5kW

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Heat Strip: Nichrome wire resistance element converting electricity to heat.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
Sequencer: Time-delay relay staging heat strips on one at a time.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: High winter electric bills often mean heat
strips running constantly because the heat pump has a problem.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Measure amp draw on each element. And — Emergency heat
costs 2-3x more than heat pump operation

00:02:37.500 --> 00:03:00.000
Take a minute before you move on. What's the one thing from this lesson you need
to remember on a service call?

